<p>
  Water damage is rarely a single event. It is a sequence: the leak, the drying, the cleanup — and then, for
  many people, a slow slide into fatigue and fogginess they cannot shake. The building got fixed.
  <strong>The body is still catching up.</strong>
</p>

<h2>Why the fog sticks around after the leak is gone</h2>
<p>
  A water-damaged building can affect people in ways that outlast the visible problem. If the moisture was not
  fully remediated — hidden cavities, drywall, carpet padding — the exposure can continue quietly, even after
  the surface looks fine. Many people report ongoing symptoms like:
</p>
<ul>
  <li>Brain fog and difficulty concentrating</li>
  <li>Fatigue that sleep does not fix</li>
  <li>Headaches or stuffiness that ease away from home</li>
  <li>Feeling worse on damp days or in certain buildings</li>
  <li>New sensitivity to smells and chemicals</li>
</ul>
<p>
  The second reason fog lingers is what happens <em>after</em>: people reach for an aggressive detox, push their
  body harder than it can clear, and end up feeling worse — then blame themselves and quit.
</p>

<h2>Step one is always the environment</h2>
<p>
  <strong>No supplement can out-detox a moldy building.</strong> Before any product, make sure the exposure has
  actually stopped: a certified inspection (not a hardware-store kit), fixing the water source, professional
  remediation when needed, humidity control and air filtration. If you cannot fix the source yet, plan around it
  with guidance rather than guessing.
</p>

<h2>Step two is measuring, not guessing</h2>
<p>
  Guessing is how people end up on the wrong detox. Through EmpowerX3's in-house, nationwide medical network,
  lab testing can be ordered and reviewed wherever you live — starting with a mycotoxin panel, the test most
  often used to check whether mold toxins are present in your body, plus any blood or genetic panels that show
  how well your body handles detox. Retesting along the way shows you your progress in numbers.
</p>

<h2>Step three is a paced, four-phase recovery</h2>
<p>
  The order matters as much as the product. EmpowerX3's Mold Recovery program runs about four months:
</p>
<ol>
  <li><strong>Weeks 1–2 · Open the exits</strong> — digestion, hydration and protein intake working before anything gets stirred up</li>
  <li><strong>Weeks 3–10 · Bind and clear</strong> — support added one piece at a time, a few days apart, to catch toxins in the gut before reabsorption</li>
  <li><strong>Weeks 6–18 · Restore the gut</strong> — clear unwanted microbes and rebuild a healthy lining and good bacteria</li>
  <li><strong>Week 18+ · Rebuild and maintain</strong> — a small daily routine and a plan for staying protected</li>
</ol>
<p>
  Pacing is the difference between finishing a recovery and abandoning it. Move toxins faster than your body can
  clear them and you feel worse, not better — that is why so many people quit. A guided program adjusts before a
  rough patch turns into a setback.
</p>

